# Carnage, Crimson Chaos's enters trigger gives the creature it returns "When this creature deals combat damage to a
# player, sacrifice it" - an ability of Carnage's card, whatever the object it resolves for has become (CR 113.7a, 603.3).
# With High Fae Trickster letting Bot1 cast spells as though they had flash (CR 702.8a), Bot1 responds to the trigger by
# casting Cubwarden on turn 9 for its mutate cost over Carnage, on top (CR 702.140c): the merged creature has Cubwarden's
# characteristics and Carnage's abilities too (CR 702.140e). The trigger then returns Memnite (discarded to Faithless
# Looting on turn 1), which gains both abilities. On turn 11 it attacks, as it must, deals 1 to Bot2, and is sacrificed.

